ift this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "The open TX-23 seat favors Republicans on paper, with a seven-point Republican partisan lean and a national environment working in the GOP's direction. Most expert raters call the race Likely Republican, though several rate it a Tossup and prediction markets put the Republican's chances near 61%. No recent high-quality general-election polls are available, so the picture rests largely on fundamentals.\n\nRepublican Brandon Herrera, a well-funded gun-content creator, has faced a steady stream of damaging coverage over crude remarks and delayed financial disclosures, and outside groups have spent heavily against him. Democrat Katy Padilla Stout has raised far less. The combination still favors the Republican, but the margin is narrower than the district's lean alone would suggest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3496, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2679, "margin": -4.5}]}